      "name": "Draining Strike",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "divine"
      ],
      "text": "When a thanadaemon damages a living creature with a melee Strike, the creature must succeed at a DC 33 Fortitude save save or become Drained 1. Further damage dealt by the thanadaemon increases the drained condition value by 1 on a failed save, to a maximum of drained 4."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Focus Gaze",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "divine",
        "fear",
        "visual"
      ],
      "text": "The thanadaemon glares at a single creature they can see within 30 feet. If the target wasn't already Frightened, they must immediately attempt a DC 33 Will save save against the thanadaemon's terrifying gaze. If the target was already frightened, they must attempt a DC 33 Will save save or become Fleeing for 1d4 rounds; this second effect has the incapacitation trait. After attempting its save, the creature is temporarily immune to this ability until the start of the thanadaemon's next turn."
    },
